<node id="1225420" title="Re: webperl: fetching data over the web" created="2018-11-08 10:15:50" updated="2018-11-08 10:15:50" _doctext_mode="strict"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="830549">haukex</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strike&gt;You're right that it has to do with async execution - the fetch happens in the background, and you can't just check &lt;c&gt;req.status&lt;/c&gt; right away - you need to register an event listener (I think you were probably just lucky in your tests that the requests returned very quickly &lt;c&gt;:-)&lt;/c&gt;&amp;nbsp;).&lt;/strike&gt; (&lt;small&gt;&lt;i&gt;Update:&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/small&gt; Oops, see replies!) See e.g. [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/XMLHttpRequest/Using_XMLHttpRequest|Using XMLHttpRequest].&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;del&gt;The second&lt;/del&gt;&lt;ins&gt;Another&lt;/ins&gt; issue &lt;ins&gt;to be aware of&lt;/ins&gt; is that scripts in the "[https://webperl.zero-g.net/democode/|democode]" page are run in a &lt;c&gt;perl&lt;/c&gt; that gets ended when the main script is done; no async stuff is possible. For that, you need to either embed &lt;c&gt;&lt;script&gt;&lt;/c&gt; tags in an HTML file, or use the "Run &amp;amp; Persist" mode of the [https://webperl.zero-g.net/using.html#the-mini-ide|"mini IDE"]. In the latter, the following works for me. (Note there are also other events on [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/XMLHttpRequest|XMLHttpRequest], such as &lt;c&gt;error&lt;/c&gt; and &lt;c&gt;abort&lt;/c&gt;.)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;c&gt;
use warnings;
use 5.028;
use WebPerl qw/js js_new/;

my $xhr = js_new('XMLHttpRequest');
$xhr-&gt;addEventListener("load", sub {
	say "Loaded! &lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;",$xhr-&gt;{responseText},"&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;\n";
});
$xhr-&gt;open("GET", "http://localhost:5000/");
say "Sending...\n";
$xhr-&gt;send();
&lt;/c&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Actually, I am currently working on a subclass of [mod://Future::HTTP] that I'd like to include by default in WebPerl to make HTTP requests easier out of the box, hopefully I can release it soon.&lt;/p&gt;</doctext>
